# Downstream cluster `${cluster_name}`

Rancher provisioned the cluster and reports it ready.

| | |
|---|---|
| Rancher | ${rancher_cluster_url} |
| Kubernetes (RKE2) | `${kubernetes_version}` |
| Region | `${region}` |
| Node egress IP | `${nat_public_ip}` |

## Node pools

| Pool | Role | Nodes |
|---|---|---|
%{ for name, p in pools ~}
| `${name}` | ${p.role} | ${p.quantity} |
%{ endfor ~}

## Access

Open the cluster in Rancher and use **Download KubeConfig**. The kubeconfig
goes through Rancher's proxy and carries your own Rancher identity; this
building block hands out no cluster credentials.

Ask the platform team for access: project and cluster permissions are granted
in Rancher.
